    "updated_at": "2024-01-25T01:28:49Z",
    "body": "Braille ASCII (also known as BRF or SimBraille) also maps 0x60-0x7e to (U+28 and leading 0 not shown) 8, 1, 3, 9, 19, 11, B, 1B, 13, A, 1A, 5, 7, D, 1D, 15, F, 1F, 17, E, 1E, 25, 27, 3A, 2D, 3D, 35, 2A, 33, 3B, and 18, just like 0x40-0x5e.",
